privateData.editorialMd:
Build runLengths

A run is a group of matching characters next to each other. End a run only when the character changes or the text ends. Record the length of each run, from left to right. Spaces count as characters too. For "aa bb", `runLengths` is [2, 1, 2].

Return the answer

Complete `ribbonRunsProofStrip` so it returns `runLengths`. Return it, do not print it.

Why this works

Each value in `runLengths` follows task 1. The later tasks use only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(n); extra memory, including the helper list, O(n). n is the input length. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

